; mdx runs the OCaml fences, except those marked skip: installation commands,
; which need the network, and the glue over rig, which needs a GPU. Shell
; examples (`munin`, `jq`, `tail`) are marked skip: they name run ids drawn
; per run and print what the reader's store holds. The guides stand for a
; crashed program with a forked child, so they do not run on Windows.

(mdx
 (files *.md)
 (package munin)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{os_type} Win32))
 (preludes prelude.ml)
 (libraries munin munin.sys unix))
